---
import FaviconLinks from '../../components/FaviconLinks.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<FaviconLinks />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
		<title>Privacy Policy — Buzbo</title>
	</head>
	<body class="font-sans antialiased text-gray-900">
		<main class="mx-auto max-w-xl px-5 py-8 sm:px-6 sm:py-10">
			<p class="mb-6 rounded-md border border-primary-mauve/30 bg-primary-mauve/10 px-3 py-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-primary-mauve">
				Pending review by NL/EU legal counsel before public launch.
			</p>

			<h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight text-primary-crimson sm:text-4xl">Buzbo Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">Last updated: 26 August 2026</p>
			<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
				Operated by AH Limited B.V., registered in the Netherlands, KVK 92705987.
				Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@buzbo.com" class="font-medium text-primary-crimson underline underline-offset-2">hello@buzbo.com</a>.
			</p>

			<article class="legal mt-8 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-800">
					<p class="mt-3">Buzbo is a human-first professional connection platform. We help professionals and business managers discover relevant people based on professional information, work preferences, ambitions, skills, and other information they choose to share.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">This Privacy Policy explains what personal data Buzbo collects, why we use it, who we share it with, how long we keep it, and what rights you have.</p>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">1. Who we are</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Buzbo is a product and project operated by <strong>AH Limited B.V.</strong>, registered in the Netherlands under KVK number <strong>92705987</strong>.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">For the purposes of applicable data protection legislation, AH Limited B.V. is currently responsible for processing personal data in connection with Buzbo.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><em>Buzbo B.V. is intended to be established as a separate company. Once Buzbo B.V. takes over responsibility for the Buzbo service, this Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly.</em></p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hello@buzbo.com" class="font-medium text-primary-crimson underline underline-offset-2">hello@buzbo.com</a></p>
					<p class="mt-3">This policy applies to the Buzbo app (iOS and Android) and buzbo.com. Event registration and ticketing is handled separately through our events partner and is covered by our Event Terms.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">2. Who can use Buzbo</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Buzbo is for professionals and business managers aged <strong>18 and over</strong>. You must not create an account if you are under 18. If we discover we've collected personal data from someone under 18, we will delete it.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">3. What Buzbo does</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Buzbo helps professionals and business managers discover and connect with people who may be relevant to their professional goals. Based on your profile and preferences, Buzbo may recommend people who match your selected criteria.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Buzbo does not make employment decisions on behalf of users.</strong> A recommendation doesn't mean a person is suitable for a job, will be hired, or will enter into any professional relationship with you. You decide whether to connect. The other person decides whether to connect.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">4. Information you provide</h2>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Account information:</strong> name; email address, if you use email-based login or provide it; phone number, if you use phone-based login or provide it; identifiers associated with Google, LinkedIn, or Apple Sign In where applicable.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Profile information:</strong> age; gender; profile photo; profession; work experience; skills; languages; about/profile text; volunteering experience; career ambitions; work preferences; what you're looking for; other information you voluntarily add to your profile.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Location information:</strong> with your permission, Buzbo uses your device's <strong>coarse (city/area-level) location</strong> to help with things like showing you relevant people and opportunities near you. Buzbo does not collect your precise GPS location. You can control location permissions in your device settings.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Messages:</strong> when you connect with another user, messages and related technical information are processed so the messaging feature can function.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Payment information:</strong> if you buy a subscription or a one-time purchase, payment is handled by Apple, Google, and RevenueCat — Buzbo does not see or store your card details.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">Buzbo does <strong>not</strong> currently collect: CV/resume uploads, voice recordings, or video.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">5. LinkedIn information</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Connecting LinkedIn is entirely optional. If you choose to use it, the flow is:</p>
					<p class="mt-3">1. You provide the URL of <strong>your own</strong> LinkedIn profile.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">2. You explicitly authorize Buzbo to retrieve information from that profile.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">3. Buzbo retrieves the available professional information and creates a <strong>draft</strong> Buzbo profile from it.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">4. You review, edit, and explicitly approve your profile before it's used or shown to anyone else.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">Depending on what's available on your profile, this may include your name, professional headline, about section, work experience, education, languages, volunteering information, and other professional information relevant to building your Buzbo profile.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">This information is used only to help build your own Buzbo profile — it is never used to create a profile of anyone else, and you're never obligated to use this feature.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">6. Company information (for Business Managers)</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Connecting your company's LinkedIn is entirely optional. If you use Buzbo as a business manager and choose to use it, the flow is:</p>
					<p class="mt-3">1. You provide the URL of your own LinkedIn Company profile.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">2. You explicitly authorize Buzbo to retrieve information from that Company profile.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">3. Buzbo retrieves the available information and creates a draft Buzbo profile from it.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">4. You review, edit, and explicitly approve your profile before it's used or shown to anyone else.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">Depending on what's available, this may include the company name and description, recent publicly available company posts, and publicly visible information about people associated with the company.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">This information is used only to help build your own Buzbo profile — it is never used to create a profile of anyone else, and you're never obligated to use this feature.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Buzbo does not create individual Buzbo accounts for people solely because they appear in this company information. The fact that someone appears as an employee or associated person in that information does not mean they've joined Buzbo or consented to receive communications from Buzbo.</strong></p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">7. AI-assisted profile creation</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Buzbo uses AI to help you and, where authorized, your LinkedIn or company information, get turned into a structured profile — both your personal Buzbo profile and, if you're a business manager, the company context described in Section 6.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>AI is used only to help create these profiles.</strong> It is not used to generate your recommendations or decide who is shown to whom — see Section 8 for how that works.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">AI-generated content is a starting point, not a guarantee of accuracy — review anything generated for you before it's used or published.</p>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>Buzbo does not use AI to:</strong></p>
					<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
						<li>make employment or hiring decisions</li>
						<li>decide who you or another user connects with</li>
						<li>create psychological or medical diagnoses</li>
						<li>infer health conditions, political opinions, religious beliefs, sexual orientation, ethnicity, or race</li>
						<li>automatically exclude anyone from the platform</li>
					</ul>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">8. Matching and recommendations</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Separately from AI-assisted profile creation, Buzbo uses a scoring system to determine which profiles are more relevant to show you, based on your profile, preferences, and other relevant information.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">This is a recommendation mechanism, not a decision-making system — it doesn't make hiring decisions and doesn't automatically exclude anyone from the platform. You always decide whether to connect, and so does the other person. Buzbo doesn't guarantee that a recommendation will result in a connection, interview, employment, freelance engagement, or any other outcome.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">9. Photos and video at events</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">At Buzbo events, we let attendees know at registration that photos and video may be taken, and may use these for marketing, social media, our website, and community communication. If you'd rather not appear in identifiable photos or video, tell us and we'll respect that. Full event-specific terms are in our Event Terms.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">10. Who we share data with</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">We don't sell your personal data. We use technical and analytics services to operate, secure, and improve Buzbo, and share information with them only for the purposes connected to what they provide. As of this policy's last update, that includes:</p>
					<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
						<li><strong>PostHog</strong> — product and in-app usage analytics</li>
						<li><strong>Sentry</strong> — crash and error reporting</li>
						<li><strong>Supabase</strong> — database and authentication infrastructure</li>
						<li><strong>Hostinger</strong> — hosts the server running our matching/scoring engine</li>
						<li><strong>GetStream</strong> — messaging infrastructure</li>
						<li><strong>AWS SES</strong> — transactional email</li>
						<li><strong>OneSignal</strong> — notifications</li>
						<li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> — subscription management</li>
						<li><strong>Apple and Google</strong> — in-app purchase processing</li>
						<li><strong>Anthropic</strong> — AI processing for profile creation</li>
						<li><strong>Luma and Stripe</strong> — event registration and payment</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="mt-3">These providers process information on Buzbo's behalf, under contract, and only for purposes connected to the service they provide. The final list and applicable processing arrangements will be maintained as Buzbo's technology stack develops. We don't give event partners attendee lists or contact details — if a partner wants to follow up with attendees, we send that communication on their behalf.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">11. International data transfers</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Some service providers are based, or run infrastructure, outside the EU/EEA and UK. This currently includes Anthropic and other US-based providers, and the server running our matching engine, hosted with <strong>Hostinger in Singapore</strong> — a country the European Commission has not recognized as providing an adequate level of data protection.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">We are assessing migrating this infrastructure to the EU. Until that's complete, where we transfer personal data outside the EU/EEA or UK, we rely on appropriate safeguards, such as the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses, to keep it protected to the same standard.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">12. Why we process your data (legal basis)</h2>
					<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
						<li><strong>Performance of a contract</strong> — account creation, your profile, matching, messaging, subscriptions and purchases.</li>
						<li><strong>Consent</strong> — location access, connecting LinkedIn, certain marketing communications.</li>
						<li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — platform security, fraud prevention, improving Buzbo, understanding usage, and (for company information) providing accurate professional context based on publicly available information.</li>
						<li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — accounting, tax, and other requirements under Dutch and EU law.</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="mt-3">You can withdraw consent at any time; this doesn't affect processing that already happened lawfully.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">13. How long we keep your data</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">We keep account and profile data for as long as your account is active. When you delete your account, we delete or anonymize your personal data within a reasonable period, except where we're legally required to retain specific records (for example, for tax purposes) for longer.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">14. Account deletion</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">You can request deletion of your account by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@buzbo.com" class="font-medium text-primary-crimson underline underline-offset-2">hello@buzbo.com</a>.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">Deleting your Buzbo account does not automatically cancel a subscription purchased through Apple or Google — you remain responsible for cancelling an active subscription through the relevant platform.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">15. Your rights</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">Depending on where you live and applicable law, you may have rights including:</p>
					<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
						<li>access to your personal data;</li>
						<li>correction of inaccurate data;</li>
						<li>deletion of personal data;</li>
						<li>restriction of processing;</li>
						<li>objection to certain processing;</li>
						<li>data portability;</li>
						<li>withdrawal of consent; and</li>
						<li>the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection authority.</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="mt-3">If you are in the Netherlands, you may contact the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens.</p>
					<p class="mt-3">To exercise your rights, contact: <a href="mailto:hello@buzbo.com" class="font-medium text-primary-crimson underline underline-offset-2">hello@buzbo.com</a></p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">16. Security</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">We use industry-standard measures, including encryption in transit and access controls, to protect your data. No system is 100% secure; we'll notify you and relevant authorities where a breach is likely to put your rights at risk, as required by law.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">17. Cookies and analytics</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">We use cookies on buzbo.com and analytics (PostHog) and crash reporting (Sentry) in the app to understand usage and keep Buzbo secure. Where required, we'll ask for consent before setting non-essential cookies.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">18. Changes</h2>
					<p class="mt-3">We may update this Privacy Policy when Buzbo changes, when our data practices change, or when required by law. The latest version will always show the applicable "Last updated" date. Where a change materially affects your rights or the way we process your personal data, we will take appropriate steps to inform you.</p>
				</section>
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl leading-snug text-primary-crimson">19. Contact</h2>
					<p class="mt-3"><strong>AH Limited B.V. — Buzbo</strong></p>
					<p class="mt-3">KVK: 92705987</p>
					<p class="mt-3">Email: <a href="mailto:hello@buzbo.com" class="font-medium text-primary-crimson underline underline-offset-2">hello@buzbo.com</a></p>
				</section>

				<p class="border-t border-primary-mauve/20 pt-6 text-sm text-gray-600">
					See also our <a href="/app/tnc" class="font-medium text-primary-crimson underline underline-offset-2">Terms & Conditions</a>.
				</p>
			</article>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
